{"key":"u13-apphycem-mcq-001-v3","kind":"mcq","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro","pass":"solve","ok":true,"object":{"chosen_label":"C","final_answer":"It stays the same","working":"By Gauss's law, the net electric flux through a closed surface depends only on the total charge enclosed: Φ_net = Q_enc/ε0. The enclosed charge remains +4.0 μC whether it is at the center or near the inside surface. The outside charge is not enclosed, so although it changes the local electric field at the surface, its net flux contribution through the closed surface is zero. Therefore the net flux is unchanged.","defect":""},"usage":{"inputTokens":492,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":108,"cacheReadTokens":384},"outputTokens":295,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":125,"reasoningTokens":170},"totalTokens":787,"raw":{"prompt_tokens":492,"completion_tokens":295,"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":384,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":108,"total_tokens":787,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":384},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":170}},"reasoningTokens":170,"cachedInputTokens":384},"attempts":1,"mode":"object","ms":3374,"keyed_label":"C"}
