{"key":"u13-apphycem-mcq-030-v1","kind":"mcq","model":"google/gemini-3.8-flash","pass":"solve","ok":true,"object":{"chosen_label":"C","final_answer":"one-fourth of its original value","working":"When the battery is disconnected after charging, the charge Q on the capacitor plates remains constant. The initial energy stored is U_0 = Q^2 / (2 C_0). Inserting a dielectric with dielectric constant κ = 4 increases the capacitance to C = κ C_0 = 4 C_0. The new energy stored in the capacitor is U = Q^2 / (2 C) = Q^2 / (2 * 4 C_0) = U_0 / 4. Thus, the stored energy becomes one-fourth of its original value.","defect":""},"usage":{"inputTokens":387,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":387,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":342,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":160,"reasoningTokens":182},"totalTokens":729,"raw":{"thoughtsTokenCount":182,"promptTokenCount":387,"candidatesTokenCount":160,"totalTokenCount":729,"trafficType":"ON_DEMAND","promptTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":387}],"candidatesTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":160}]},"reasoningTokens":182,"cachedInputTokens":0},"attempts":1,"mode":"object","ms":2834,"keyed_label":"C"}
