{"key":"u13-apphycem-mcq-029-v1","kind":"mcq","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro","pass":"solve","ok":true,"object":{"chosen_label":"D","final_answer":"A component along the surface would push charges along it, so equilibrium allows none","working":"In electrostatic equilibrium, the charges on a conductor are at rest. If the electric field just outside the surface had a tangential component, it would exert a tangential force on mobile surface charges. That force would cause charges to move along the surface, producing a surface current and violating the electrostatic equilibrium condition. Therefore, equilibrium requires the exterior field to have no tangential component, leaving only a perpendicular component at the surface.","defect":""},"usage":{"inputTokens":460,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":76,"cacheReadTokens":384},"outputTokens":411,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":126,"reasoningTokens":285},"totalTokens":871,"raw":{"prompt_tokens":460,"completion_tokens":411,"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":384,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":76,"total_tokens":871,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":384},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":285}},"reasoningTokens":285,"cachedInputTokens":384},"attempts":1,"mode":"object","ms":5007,"keyed_label":"D"}
{"key":"u13-apphycem-mcq-030-v1","kind":"mcq","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro","pass":"solve","ok":true,"object":{"chosen_label":"C","final_answer":"one-fourth of its original value","working":"After charging, the battery is disconnected, so the charge Q on the capacitor plates remains constant. Initial energy is U_i = Q^2/(2C). Inserting a dielectric with dielectric constant κ = 4 increases the capacitance to C' = κC = 4C. The final energy is U_f = Q^2/(2C') = Q^2/(2·4C) = (1/4) Q^2/(2C) = U_i/4. Therefore, the stored energy becomes one-fourth of its original value.","defect":""},"usage":{"inputTokens":442,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":58,"cacheReadTokens":384},"outputTokens":326,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":149,"reasoningTokens":177},"totalTokens":768,"raw":{"prompt_tokens":442,"completion_tokens":326,"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":384,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":58,"total_tokens":768,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":384},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":177}},"reasoningTokens":177,"cachedInputTokens":384},"attempts":1,"mode":"object","ms":3465,"keyed_label":"C"}
{"key":"u13-apphycem-mcq-np1-003-v2","kind":"mcq","model":"google/gemini-3.8-flash","pass":"solve","ok":true,"object":{"chosen_label":"D","final_answer":"2.0 V/m in the +x direction","working":"The relationship between the electric field component and the electric potential along the x-axis is given by E_x = -dV/dx. In the region 2.0 m < x < 5.0 m, the potential decreases linearly from 10 V to 4.0 V. Thus, the derivative dV/dx = (4.0 V - 10 V) / (5.0 m - 2.0 m) = -6.0 V / 3.0 m = -2.0 V/m. Taking the negative of this derivative gives E_x = -(-2.0 V/m) = +2.0 V/m. The positive sign indicates that the electric field points in the +x direction, which matches choice D.","defect":""},"usage":{"inputTokens":457,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":457,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":606,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":209,"reasoningTokens":397},"totalTokens":1063,"raw":{"thoughtsTokenCount":397,"promptTokenCount":457,"candidatesTokenCount":209,"totalTokenCount":1063,"trafficType":"ON_DEMAND","promptTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":457}],"candidatesTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":209}]},"reasoningTokens":397,"cachedInputTokens":0},"attempts":1,"mode":"object","ms":4021,"keyed_label":"D"}
{"key":"u13-apphycem-mcq-np1-003-v2","kind":"mcq","model":"google/gemini-3.8-flash","pass":"audit","ok":true,"object":{"keyed_choice_correct":true,"per_choice":[{"label":"A","rationale_accurate":true,"issue":""},{"label":"B","rationale_accurate":true,"issue":""},{"label":"C","rationale_accurate":true,"issue":""},{"label":"D","rationale_accurate":true,"issue":""}],"other_defects":[]},"usage":{"inputTokens":805,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":805,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":884,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":154,"reasoningTokens":730},"totalTokens":1689,"raw":{"thoughtsTokenCount":730,"promptTokenCount":805,"candidatesTokenCount":154,"totalTokenCount":1689,"trafficType":"ON_DEMAND","promptTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":805}],"candidatesTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":154}]},"reasoningTokens":730,"cachedInputTokens":0},"attempts":1,"mode":"object","ms":5235,"keyed_label":"D"}
{"key":"u13-apphycem-mcq-np1-003-v2","kind":"mcq","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro","pass":"solve","ok":true,"object":{"chosen_label":"D","final_answer":"2.0 V/m in the +x direction","working":"The electric field component along x is E_x = -dV/dx. In the region 2.0 m < x < 5.0 m, the potential decreases linearly from 10 V to 4 V. Thus dV/dx = (4.0 V - 10 V)/(5.0 m - 2.0 m) = -2.0 V/m. Therefore E_x = -(-2.0 V/m) = +2.0 V/m, so the electric field is 2.0 V/m in the +x direction.","defect":""},"usage":{"inputTokens":507,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":123,"cacheReadTokens":384},"outputTokens":326,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":157,"reasoningTokens":169},"totalTokens":833,"raw":{"prompt_tokens":507,"completion_tokens":326,"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":384,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":123,"total_tokens":833,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":384},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":169}},"reasoningTokens":169,"cachedInputTokens":384},"attempts":1,"mode":"object","ms":3223,"keyed_label":"D"}
