{"key":"u13-apphycem-mcq-np1-006-v1","kind":"mcq","model":"google/gemini-3.8-flash","pass":"solve","ok":true,"object":{"chosen_label":"B","final_answer":"E_s/3","working":"For a uniformly charged solid insulating sphere of radius R carrying total charge Q, Gauss's law gives the electric field magnitude at a radial distance r <= R inside the sphere as E(r) = (1 / (4*pi*epsilon_0)) * (Q * r / R^3). At the surface r = R, E(R) = E_s = (1 / (4*pi*epsilon_0)) * (Q / R^2). Therefore, E(r) = E_s * (r / R). Evaluating at r = R/3 gives E(R/3) = E_s * (1/3) = E_s/3.","defect":""},"usage":{"inputTokens":389,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":389,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":519,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":184,"reasoningTokens":335},"totalTokens":908,"raw":{"thoughtsTokenCount":335,"promptTokenCount":389,"candidatesTokenCount":184,"totalTokenCount":908,"trafficType":"ON_DEMAND","promptTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":389}],"candidatesTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":184}]},"reasoningTokens":335,"cachedInputTokens":0},"attempts":1,"mode":"object","ms":4015,"keyed_label":"B"}
