{"key":"u13-apphycem-mcq-np1-006-v1","kind":"mcq","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro","pass":"solve","ok":true,"object":{"chosen_label":"B","final_answer":"E_s/3","working":"For a uniformly charged insulating sphere, inside at radius r the enclosed charge is proportional to r^3: Q_enc = Q(r^3/R^3). By Gauss's law, E(r) = (1/(4πε0)) Q_enc / r^2 = (1/(4πε0)) Q r / R^3. At the surface r=R, E_s = (1/(4πε0)) Q / R^2. Therefore E(r) = E_s (r/R). Setting r=R/3 gives E = E_s / 3.","defect":""},"usage":{"inputTokens":440,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":56,"cacheReadTokens":384},"outputTokens":526,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":152,"reasoningTokens":374},"totalTokens":966,"raw":{"prompt_tokens":440,"completion_tokens":526,"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":384,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":56,"total_tokens":966,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":384},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":374}},"reasoningTokens":374,"cachedInputTokens":384},"attempts":1,"mode":"object","ms":5410,"keyed_label":"B"}
